From 1a185bc9c3f1d7c5504a66c3d6cc4e3de94a31f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baricco <38298051+Baricco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:53:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] install: apply the SIGFM matching fixes to the libfprint
 fork

The SIGFM copy in the goodix-fp-linux-dev fork has two matching bugs:

- match::operator< compares only p1.y, so std::set keeps one
  correspondence per keypoint row and drops the others;
- correspondences displaced by <= 2 px come from the sensor's fixed
  pattern, which sits on the same pixels in every frame whatever the
  finger, so they match across different fingers with a perfectly
  consistent geometry.

With the image pipeline and ridge gate of the false-accepts commit our
impostor presses already score 0, so these fixes are a second line of
defence. On weak, pattern-dominated frames from the old pipeline the
unpatched SIGFM accepts 15/20 impostors (scores up to 13,256 against a
threshold of 20) and the patched one 0/20; those frames carry almost no
ridge signal, so genuine ones fail too, which is why the gate now asks
for a retry. On frames from the new pipeline the fixes leave acceptance
unchanged and raise genuine scores (median best score 5,275 -> 13,168).

Both fixes are proposed upstream on libfprint !530. Until the fork has
them, step 3 of the installers applies them to sigfm.cpp, idempotently
and with the same anchor checks as the meson patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/libfprint-integration.md |  2 ++
 install-goodixgf-en.sh        | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 install-goodixgf.sh           | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/libfprint-integration.md b/docs/libfprint-integration.md
index 4dcd989..b6e671e 100644
--- a/docs/libfprint-integration.md
+++ b/docs/libfprint-integration.md
@@ -73,6 +73,8 @@
 
    - **`libfprint/meson.build`**：`driver_sources` 用数组格式，追加 `'goodixgf'` 条目（`goodixgf.c` + `core/*.c`）。驱动类型函数 `fpi_device_goodixgf_get_type` 由构建系统按 `-Ddrivers=goodixgf` 自动收集（`drivers_type_func`），与 `goodixgf.c` 的 `G_DEFINE_TYPE` 对应。
 
+   - **`libfprint/sigfm/sigfm.cpp`**：两处匹配修复（已向上游 libfprint !530 提交，fork 合入前由脚本应用）：`match::operator<` 改为完整的字典序（原来只比较 `p1.y`，`std::set` 每行只留一个对应）；丢弃位移 ≤ 2 像素的对应（传感器固定图案在每帧同一像素，会让不同手指高分互配）。
+
 4. 编译安装：
 
    ```sh
diff --git a/install-goodixgf-en.sh b/install-goodixgf-en.sh
index 629ce5d..7e6b50e 100644
--- a/install-goodixgf-en.sh
+++ b/install-goodixgf-en.sh
@@ -19,7 +19,8 @@
 # Process:
 #   1. Install build dependencies (including opencv4 >= 4.5, doctest) + fprintd
 #   2. Copy goodixgf driver + protocol core to <source>/libfprint/drivers/goodixgf/
-#   3. Patch meson.build (fork's driver_sources / optional_deps, idempotent)
+#   3. Patch meson.build (fork's driver_sources / optional_deps) and apply the
+#      SIGFM matching fixes, idempotent
 #   4. Compile and install to /usr (SONAME unchanged, system fprintd reuses directly)
 #   5. Reload udev, restart fprintd (kept alive via --no-timeout drop-in)
 #
@@ -252,8 +253,8 @@ else
   done
 fi
 
-# ---------------- 3. Patch meson (idempotent, anchors match fork's actual structure) ----------------
-echo "==> [3/5] Patching meson.build"
+# ---------------- 3. Patch meson + SIGFM (idempotent, anchors match fork's actual structure) ----------------
+echo "==> [3/5] Patching meson.build and SIGFM"
 python3 - "$SRC" <<'PYEOF'
 import sys
 
@@ -341,7 +342,51 @@ endif"""
                  "please manually add opencv5 fallback to sigfm/meson.build")
     s = s.replace(old, new, 1)
     open(p, 'w').write(s)
-print('patched: optional_deps + driver_sources (goodixgf) + sigfm opencv fallback')
+
+# --- 3d. sigfm/sigfm.cpp: two matching fixes against false accepts ---
+# Proposed upstream on libfprint !530; applied here until the fork has them.
+# 1. match::operator< compared only p1.y, so std::set kept one correspondence
+#    per keypoint row and silently dropped the others.
+# 2. Correspondences displaced by <= 2 px come from the sensor's fixed pattern
+#    (same pixels in every frame, whatever the finger), not from the finger:
+#    without this filter impostor frames scored 2,000-13,000 against a
+#    threshold of 20.
+p = src + '/libfprint/sigfm/sigfm.cpp'
+s = orig = open(p).read()
+old = """        return (this->p1.y < right.p1.y) ||
+               ((this->p1.y < right.p1.y) && this->p1.x < right.p1.x);
+"""
+new = """        return std::tie(p1.y, p1.x, p2.y, p2.x) <
+               std::tie(right.p1.y, right.p1.x, right.p2.y, right.p2.x);
+"""
+s = s.replace(old, new, 1)
+if 'min_displacement' not in s:
+    fixes = [
+        ("constexpr auto min_match = 5;\n",
+         """constexpr auto min_match = 5;
+// Correspondences whose keypoints sit at (almost) the same sensor pixel come
+// from the sensor's fixed pattern, not from the finger: they are dropped.
+constexpr auto min_displacement = 2.0;
+"""),
+        ("""                matches_unique.emplace(
+                    match{frame->keypoints.at(match_1.queryIdx).pt,
+                          enrolled->keypoints.at(match_1.trainIdx).pt});
+""",
+         """                const cv::Point2f& kp1 = frame->keypoints.at(match_1.queryIdx).pt;
+                const cv::Point2f& kp2 = enrolled->keypoints.at(match_1.trainIdx).pt;
+                if (cv::norm(kp1 - kp2) <= min_displacement)
+                    continue;
+                matches_unique.emplace(match{kp1, kp2});
+"""),
+    ]
+    for old, new in fixes:
+        if old not in s:
+            sys.exit("!! Cannot find SIGFM matching anchors in sigfm/sigfm.cpp (fork structure changed?), "
+                     "please apply the two fixes described above step 3d manually")
+        s = s.replace(old, new, 1)
+if s != orig:
+    open(p, 'w').write(s)
+print('patched: optional_deps + driver_sources (goodixgf) + sigfm opencv fallback + sigfm matching fixes')
 PYEOF
 
 # ---------------- 4. Compile and install ----------------
